WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.920
Identify and Protect are closely connected.

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:07.220
Identify helps an organization understand what exists, what matters,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.600
and where risk may be present.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:16.380
That includes assets, systems, data, users, suppliers, business processes,

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:21.160
vulnerabilities, threats, dependencies, and operational context.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.860
You cannot protect what you do not know exists,

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.960
and you cannot prioritize risk if you do not understand which assets and outcomes matter

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.060
most.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:35.160
A practical Identify activity might involve asset inventory, data classification,

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:40.260
supplier mapping, business impact analysis, vulnerability management, or risk registers.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:43.920
The point is not to create perfect documentation that never changes.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:48.940
The point is to maintain enough current understanding that decisions are based on reality.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:53.480
If a critical system is missing from inventory, a supplier dependency is unknown,

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:58.180
or sensitive data is not recognized, the organization may underestimate risk.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.280
Protect focuses on safeguards that reduce risk.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.620
Common examples include identity management, access control, awareness training,

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:12.280
data security, platform security, secure configuration, infrastructure resilience,

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.140
and policy-backed operational procedures.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.360
Protect does not mean every safeguard is equally important everywhere.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:24.460
A target outcome should connect to the system's purpose, risk tolerance,

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.280
and threat context.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:29.300
Protection is stronger when identification is accurate.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:34.400
An access control improvement depends on knowing the users, roles, and data involved.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:39.020
A platform security improvement depends on knowing which platforms exist and who owns

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.040
them.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:44.660
A resilience improvement depends on understanding critical services and recovery needs.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:50.080
Together, Identify and Protect turn vague concern into scoped, owned,

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.780
and evidence-backed improvement work.
